  * 1.3.2 - fix: several `self._interred` presence checks used truthiness (`if self._interred:`) instead of `is not None` - since Config subclasses dict, a freshly-constructed-but-still-empty secrets Config is falsy, so _unmask() (and _locked()/_watched_files()) silently treated a real, attached secrets store as absent and skipped reloading/locking it. Concurrent first-ever construction against a not-yet-populated secrets file could leave a losing thread/process stuck seeing the mask placeholder forever instead of the real value another racer had already written. Also adds `mask_fields` (Config constructor kwarg): registers masked keys before the first load(), so a fresh install's first-ever self-dump (triggered by FileNotFoundError, before any mask() call is possible) is masked from the start instead of writing secrets to filepath in plaintext once before anyone calls mask()
  * 1.3.1 - fix: file lock is now correctly thread-scoped, not just process-scoped (cross-thread contention on one Config was silently unlocked); mask() now holds the lock for its full stage+persist cycle
  * 1.3 - cross-process file locking for load/dump
  * 1.2 - automatic+dynamic reloading of YAML files
  * 1.1 - make default, modified, and unused properties explicit in plaintext
  * 1.0 - secrets store in encrypted location
  * 0.9 - secrets store in separate location
